# Brief

## Input (quoted)
> 做一个单屏网页小游戏：方向键控制小球吃星星，30 秒倒计时，记录最高分，打开 index.html 就能玩。背景用一张位图 PNG。能玩的 build 打成 zip（解压后 index.html 在根目录）作为 release 文件发布；每个岗位把自己在浏览器里按键试玩时的截图也作为 release 文件发布。

## What the game must be
- Single-screen web game; open `index.html` directly (file://, no server, no network, no build step) and play.
- Arrow keys move a ball; touching a star eats it (+score) and a new star appears.
- 30 s countdown shown on screen; at 0 the round ends, final score shown, restart key available.
- Best score persisted (localStorage, with in-memory fallback if unavailable) and shown on screen.
- Background is one bitmap PNG, loaded by `index.html` from `assets/bg.png` (relative path, works from file://). Ball and stars may be drawn in canvas/CSS.

## Split (see assignment.json)
- game-developer: repo root = `index.html` + code, quality checks, the playable zip (index.html at zip root, includes assets/bg.png) published as a release file in its repo, plus its own browser key-press screenshot as a release file.
- artist: `assets/bg.png` (real PNG bitmap, ~800x600 or 16:10-ish, dark/low-contrast so ball and stars stay readable, no text), its own in-browser screenshot release file.
- playtester: plays the zip build in a browser with real key presses, reports, publishes screenshots as release files.
- producer: brief, assignment, acceptance, own in-browser screenshot of the build as a release file.

## Priorities
1. Playable loop works end to end (move, eat, timer, game over, best score, restart).
2. PNG background present and actually shown.
3. Zip release is correct (index.html at root, works unzipped).
4. Every position's screenshot published as a release file.

## Acceptance standard
I approve only when: zip downloaded and unzipped, index.html at root, opens and plays via arrow keys; timer counts 30 s; stars give score; best score persists across reload; background is a real PNG (file header checked) and visible; playtester has played that same zip build and reported; all four positions have a screenshot release file.

## Not established
- Exact viewport size and ball/star art style: left to game-developer/artist; the PNG size must match the canvas or be scaled by the code.
